body:
At the last GDExtension team meeting, we discussed whether or not we want to support loading GDExtensions from system paths, and the consensus among those present was that we do not.

I know we already sort of do, because of [this code](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/drivers/unix/os_unix.cpp#L888-891):

```c++
	if (!FileAccess::exists(path)) {
		// This code exists so GDExtension can load .so files from a standard unix location.
		path = get_executable_path().get_base_dir().path_join("../lib").path_join(p_path.get_file());
	}
```

It looks in `"../lib"`, and so if the Godot executeable is in `/usr/bin`, it will look in `/usr/lib`. And the comment implies (although, it's a little ambiguous) that it was added in order to support loading GDExtensions from system paths.

This code goes all the way back to 6e2ed15ff14efe3063f66c182218f56e557bb468 for GDNative from 2018, and was carried over in the conversion to GDExtension. We've learned a lot of about how both GDNative and GDExtension are used since that time, and I don't think we would choose to include this if we were evaluating it as a new feature today.

At the meeting we discussed the possibility of removing this code (I would personally be for it!) but others present at the meeting were reluctant to go that far. We discussed that at the very least, we should update the comment to state that this code is left in for compatibility, but that it's deprecated, and we don't advise loading GDExtensions from system paths. Or, we could even give a runtime message to that effect.

Anyway, as it pertains to this PR, I don't think we should _expand_ our support for loading GDExtensions from system paths.

That said, not everyone was present at the last GDExtension meeting, and it would be valuable to get input from folks outside of the team too (especially if there is anyone already relying on GDExtensions being loaded from `"../lib"`), so we can continue to discuss here :-)
